---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StatusGovernance from "../components/StatusGovernance.astro";
import ProjectUpdates from "../components/ProjectUpdates.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Unity House" description="Unity House is a proposed community-centre model from Visio Nova Mundi CIC, focused on reducing waste, affordable food access, reuse and connections between neighbours. It is in research and development.">
  <section class="heroBlock">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Research and development · CIC-led</p>
      <h1>Unity House</h1>
      <p class="lead">Unity House is a proposed community-centre model focused on reducing waste, supporting affordable food access, encouraging reuse and strengthening connections between neighbours.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#pilot-2026">What happened in 2026</a><a class="btn" href="#community-engagement">Register your interest</a></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="statusCard vnm-glass-card"><p class="statusLabel">Current status</p><h2>Research and development</h2><p>A six-session health-and-wellbeing pilot was developed in 2026 but did not proceed. We are using the planning experience to refine the model and explore future partnerships and funding.</p><span class="statusPill">No centre or delivery programme confirmed</span></aside>
  </section>

  <StatusGovernance stage="Research and development" operator="Visio Nova Mundi CIC — CIC-led programme" delivery="No current delivery. A six-session health-and-wellbeing pilot developed in 2026 did not proceed, and no sessions took place." partnership="No institutional partnership or endorsement is implied." funding="No current programme funding." boundary="Unity House is a model under development. There is no permanent centre, public waste-collection service or active food-surplus operation." />

  <figure class="project-concept-visual">
    <img src="/images/unity-house-concept.webp" alt="Concept visual of a proposed future Unity House community hub, with neighbours cooking and learning together; it does not depict an operating centre." loading="eager" decoding="async" width="1536" height="1024" data-project-image />
    <figcaption>Concept visual · future Unity House Centres model</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="section communityUpdate" id="pilot-2026">
    <p class="eyebrow">The 2026 pilot · not delivered</p><h2>What we developed, and why it matters now</h2>
    <p>In 2026 we developed a six-session community health and wellbeing pilot for adults, focused on healthy eating, affordable food choices and social connection, with Romanian-English access. Food would have come from an appropriately registered provider, where authorised, rather than being cooked during sessions.</p>
    <p>The pilot did not proceed and no sessions took place. Planning it showed us what any future Unity House activity needs in place before it starts: a suitable venue, competent facilitation, safeguarding, food-safety arrangements and insurance. That learning is shaping the next version of the model.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section modelIntro">
    <div class="sectionHead">
      <p class="eyebrow">Long-term concept study</p>
      <p><strong>Long-term conceptual study. Any first phase would use existing community venues rather than a new building.</strong></p>
      <h2>A community house that turns local resources into community value</h2>
      <p>The longer-term vision is a neighbourhood circular-economy hub: a trusted place where suitable local surplus, reusable materials and appropriate waste streams can be brought together and managed responsibly.</p>
      <p>Small, bounded pilots would be the first real-world tests of the model. Each would generate learning about community health, food, reuse and connection, and that evidence would guide any step toward a permanent neighbourhood hub.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="modelGrid">
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Affordable meals from surplus</h3><p>Where food is legally sourced and safe to use, suitable edible surplus could become affordable meals, subject to lawful food-handling arrangements and partners.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Reuse, repair and upcycling</h3><p>Reusable materials could be sorted into repair, upcycling, sharing or other routes that keep useful resources in community use.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Appropriate treatment</h3><p>Unavoidable food waste could go to appropriate composting or other authorised treatment through competent partners.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Jobs, learning and belonging</h3><p>The wider model aims to create local jobs and training, support volunteering and help neighbours from different communities meet and work together.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="safeguard"><strong>Statutory boundary:</strong> Any future collection, storage, transport, preparation, redistribution or treatment would need separate scope, responsible partners and the relevant food-safety, waste, environmental-permitting, planning, insurance, safeguarding and data-protection controls.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section communityUpdate" id="community-engagement">
    <p class="eyebrow">Future activity</p>
    <h2>Help shape what comes next</h2>
    <p>We would like to hear from residents, community organisations and potential hosts who could help us understand local needs and design a future pilot responsibly. Any future activity would be health promotion and signposting, not clinical advice, diagnosis or treatment.</p>
    <p>We are also interested in hearing from <strong>Romanian-speaking and Romanian-English volunteers and community connectors</strong> who might help with communication, introductions and gathering community feedback if a future pilot goes ahead.</p>
    <div class="volunteerRow">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Interested in helping?</p>
        <p class="volunteerBoundary">Registering interest does not commit you to anything. Volunteer roles would support communication, welcoming residents and simple feedback collection; they are community-support roles, not clinical or professional nutrition roles.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn primary" href="/contact/">Contact Visio Nova Mundi</a>
    </div>
    <p class="safeguard"><strong>No delivery programme is currently confirmed. Unity House does not operate a permanent centre, a public waste-collection service or a food-surplus operation.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
    <p class="eyebrow">How we will learn</p>
      <h2>Community insight before larger claims</h2>
      <p>In any future pilot, participants may be invited, with informed consent, to complete short feedback forms or share their views in a conversation. We would ask only for information needed to understand opinions, access barriers and what support residents value.</p>
      <p>Responses would be handled under an agreed privacy notice and safeguarding process. Participation would be voluntary, and feedback would not determine eligibility for services or support.</p>
      <p class="note"><strong>Community insights would support evaluation of each pilot and inform feasibility work for any future Unity House centre.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="sectionHead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Future Unity House Centres model</p>
      <h2>Local proof first, potential UK replication later</h2>
      <p>The wider Unity House model is intended to be locally adaptable rather than dependent on one locality or building. A permanent neighbourhood hub or wider UK network would only be considered after credible evidence, partners, permissions and sustainable resources are in place.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flow"><div><strong>1</strong><span>One evidenced local need</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>One trusted host</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>One suitable resource stream</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>Appropriate partners</span></div><div><strong>5</strong><span>Responsible coordination</span></div><div><strong>6</strong><span>Evidence and learning</span></div></div>
    <p class="formula">1 evidenced local need + 1 trusted host + 1 suitable resource stream + appropriate partners + responsible evidence = 1 testable local Unity House node</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid section">
    <article class="card highlight vnm-glass-card"><p class="eyebrow">Possible future activity</p><h2>Healthy eating and cultural connection</h2><p>Future activity could explore Romanian-English healthy eating, affordable food choices, shared learning and connection between people from Romanian, British, Polish and other local communities. Any surplus-food, collection or processing activity would require an appropriate host, food-safety controls and the required approvals.</p></article>
    <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><p class="eyebrow">Future community exchange</p><h2>Bringing people together safely</h2><p>Subject to consent, safeguarding and partner approval, future activities could include hosted cultural visits, intergenerational gatherings, park walks, cooking sessions and companionship for older people who feel isolated. No home visits or exchanges would take place without formal risk assessment and clear participant protections.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section class="section boundary">
    <div class="sectionHead"><p class="eyebrow">Responsible development</p><h2>Clear scope for any future pilot or centre</h2><p>Any future pilot would follow an agreed scope and the requirements of its host venue and any funder. A permanent centre or any collection, food-handling or waste-treatment activity would need its own partners, resources, permissions and readiness checks.</p><p class="note"><strong>Unity House is designed to connect with and learn from community organisations already working locally.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="cards four"><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No centre yet</h3><p>There is no Unity House building, delivery programme or UK-wide network.</p></article><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No automatic waste handling</h3><p>Future resource streams would need separate partners, permissions and lawful treatment routes.</p></article><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No clinical service</h3><p>Any future activity would provide health promotion and signposting, not diagnosis, treatment or clinical advice.</p></article><article class="smallCard vnm-glass-card"><h3>No invented outcomes</h3><p>Learning and participant feedback would be reported within each pilot's evidence and consent boundaries.</p></article></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section supportBar vnm-glass-card"><div><h2>Would you like to get involved?</h2><p>We are looking for careful conversations with residents, volunteers, community connectors and potential hosts who can help us understand local needs responsibly.</p></div><a class="btn primary" href="/contact/">Contact Visio Nova Mundi</a></section>

  <style>
    .heroBlock{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.25fr .75fr;gap:18px;align-items:start}.eyebrow{margin:0 0 9px;color:#0f766e;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}h1{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,64px);letter-spacing:-.04em;color:var(--text)}.lead{margin:0;max-width:72ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:19px}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-radius:14px;padding:11px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:white;color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font-weight:850}.btn.primary{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.10),rgba(16,185,129,.10));border-color:rgba(39,99,235,.25)}.btn:hover{border-color:rgba(0,0,0,.18);text-decoration:none}.statusCard,.card,.smallCard,.supportBar{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:18px;background:white;box-shadow:0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.05)}.statusCard{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.07),rgba(16,185,129,.07))}.statusCard.vnm-glass-card,.card.vnm-glass-card,.smallCard.vnm-glass-card,.supportBar.vnm-glass-card{border-color:rgba(37,99,235,.2);background-image:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(37,99,235,.12),rgba(16,185,129,.10));background-color:var(--glass);box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(37,99,235,.12),inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.64);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(20px) saturate(130%);backdrop-filter:blur(20px) saturate(130%);color:var(--text)}.statusCard.vnm-glass-card h2,.card.vnm-glass-card h2,.smallCard.vnm-glass-card h3,.supportBar.vnm-glass-card h2{color:var(--text)}.statusCard.vnm-glass-card p,.card.vnm-glass-card p,.smallCard.vnm-glass-card p,.supportBar.vnm-glass-card p{color:var(--muted)}.statusLabel{margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}.statusCard h2,.card h2,.supportBar h2{margin:0 0 9px;color:var(--text);font-size:21px;letter-spacing:-.02em}.statusCard p,.card p,.smallCard p,.supportBar p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.statusPill{display:inline-block;margin-top:14px;padding:7px 10px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.28);color:#0f766e;font-size:12px;font-weight:850;background:rgba(16,185,129,.08)}.section{margin-top:34px}.sectionHead h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:29px;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--text)}.sectionHead>p:not(.eyebrow){margin:0;max-width:90ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.sectionHead>.note{margin-top:12px!important;font-size:13px}.modelIntro{padding:22px;border:1px solid rgba(37,99,235,.2);border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(37,99,235,.08),rgba(16,185,129,.08))}.modelIntro .sectionHead>p:not(.eyebrow)+p{margin-top:12px}.modelGrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:16px}.modelGrid .card{padding:15px}.modelGrid .card h3{margin:0 0 7px;color:var(--text);font-size:16px}.modelGrid .card p{font-size:14px}.communityUpdate{padding:22px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.24);border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(16,185,129,.08),rgba(39,99,235,.06))}.communityUpdate h2{margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--text);font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.025em}.communityUpdate>p:not(.eyebrow):not(.safeguard){color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.volunteerRow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;margin-top:18px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.2)}.volunteerBoundary{margin:0;max-width:72ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.safeguard{margin:18px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border-left:3px solid #d97706;background:rgba(245,158,11,.09);color:var(--text)!important;line-height:1.7}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;align-items:start}.highlight{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.06))}.note{margin-top:12px!important;font-size:13px}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:16px}.flow div{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:13px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(39,99,235,.04);color:var(--text);font-weight:750}.flow strong{display:grid;place-items:center;flex:0 0 28px;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(39,99,235,.12);color:#0e6b63}.formula{margin:14px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.18);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(16,185,129,.06);color:var(--text);line-height:1.6;font-weight:750}.boundary{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:25px}.cards.four{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:14px}.smallCard{padding:14px}.smallCard h3{margin:0 0 7px;color:var(--text);font-size:16px}.smallCard p{font-size:14px}.supportBar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.06))}.supportBar>div{max-width:75ch}.controlNote{margin:18px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border-left:3px solid #d97706;background:rgba(245,158,11,.09);color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;font-size:13px}@media(max-width:1100px){.flow,.modelGrid{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:900px){.heroBlock,.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.flow,.cards.four,.modelGrid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.supportBar,.volunteerRow{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch}}@media(max-width:520px){.flow,.cards.four,.modelGrid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.communityUpdate{padding:18px}.supportBar{padding:16px}.btn{width:100%}}
  </style>
  <ProjectUpdates project="unity-house" />
</BaseLayout>
